Eli (docs): Quick suggestion: add a compact decision diagram to the error-ref for 429s/timeouts/context-limits. People keep asking which fallback runs first.
Jo (eng-runtime): Agreed. Visual + 2 SDK snippets should clear up most questions. Note: streaming is a special case.
Priya (devex): I can drop a tiny Mermaid block in the PR. Draft: ```mermaid
flowchart TD
  R[Request] --> T{Error type}
  T -- 429 --> Retry[Client retry + backoff]
  T -- timeout --> Trim[Trim/summarize & retry]
  Retry --> Check{Still throttled?}
  Check -- yes --> Model[Model variant fallback]
  Model --> Region[Regional failover]
  Check -- no --> OK[Success]
```
Sam (eng-ml): Add callouts for triggers: 429=rate, timeout=latency, queue-depth=backpressure. Also a short note about KV cache mismatch when switching quantized variants.
Eli (docs): I'll open a PR with the mermaid + brief prose and an FAQ line: "When should I retry vs trim?". Priya, can you add JS/Python snippets for Retry-After parsing + decorrelated jitter?
Priya (devex): Yep. Short JS example: ```js
async function fetchWithRetry(req, attempts=4){
  for(let i=0;i<attempts;i++){
    const r = await fetch(req);
    if(r.status===429){
      const ra = parseInt(r.headers.get('Retry-After')||'0',10);
      const wait = ra>0? ra*1000 : Math.min(60000, (2**i)*100 + Math.random()*200);
      await new Promise(s=>setTimeout(s, wait));
      continue;
    }
    return r;
  }
  throw new Error('max-retries');
}
```
Jo (eng-runtime): I'll review and add an infra test that simulates cascading 429s to validate the docs ordering. For streaming, call out resume tokens and X-Resume-Offset header.
